Z||000000||Philphine||10-20-2001||09:25 PM||||<BR>i was doing the weekend wander killing time and stopped in a local speed/custom shop. one of the workers asks if i'd like to see the owners fiero. it's being painted in the back.<P>!!!<P>"uh..ok"<P>this is a shop i've been in and out of plenty of times, most of the time in my fiero. never knew the owner had one, but then i don't know who the owner is to know if i've met him. go back and see a gt with no facias being prepped. the owners not there. walk around back and there they are. 2-5" tips on each side. i didn't think there was enough room but he shows me the unaltered facia. i know what you're thinking but i don't think you could get a more agressive look, and he said it sounded great. just had a stock v6 (by appearance anyway) though. i think i'd want more to back up that look.<P>also had a front trunk full of amps but i didn't get to see the interior to see what they were powering. left the forum addy so i hope he shows up (i'm batting 0 so far. hope to talk to him personally also. the owner of a custom shop that owns a fiero has got to be a positive.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
